  "lines": [
   {
    "i": 0,
    "start": 0.06,
    "end": 3.9715833333333332,
    "text": "If you press the button in front of you, you'll win fifty thousand dollars."
   },
   {
    "i": 1,
    "start": 4.14,
    "end": 5.8189166666666665,
    "text": "But someone you don't know will die."
   },
   {
    "i": 2,
    "start": 6.179999999999999,
    "end": 7.356208333333332,
    "text": "You won't see who it is."
   },
   {
    "i": 3,
    "start": 7.829999999999999,
    "end": 9.07025,
    "text": "You won't even learn their name."
   },
   {
    "i": 4,
    "start": 9.579999999999998,
    "end": 10.832166666666666,
    "text": "Would you press it?"
   },
   {
    "i": 5,
    "start": 11.00333333333333,
    "end": 17.486749999999997,
    "text": "Richard Matheson's story \"Button, Button,\" published in 1970, puts you face to face with exactly this kind of offer."
   },
   {
    "i": 6,
    "start": 18.283333333333328,
    "end": 21.664499999999993,
    "text": "A package is left at the door of Norma and Arthur, who live in New York."
   },
   {
    "i": 7,
    "start": 22.443333333333328,
    "end": 24.352583333333328,
    "text": "Inside is a small wooden box."
   },
   {
    "i": 8,
    "start": 25.00333333333333,
    "end": 28.65033333333333,
    "text": "On top of the box, under a locked glass cover, there's a single button."
   },
   {
    "i": 9,
    "start": 29.623333333333328,
    "end": 32.59783333333333,
    "text": "The note next to it says a Mr. Steward will come by at eight p.m."
   },
   {
    "i": 10,
    "start": 33.763333333333335,
    "end": 37.650958333333335,
    "text": "When Steward arrives, he leaves the key on the table and explains his offer."
   },
   {
    "i": 11,
    "start": 38.13333333333333,
    "end": 41.74191666666667,
    "text": "If they press the button, they'll get fifty thousand dollars."
   },
   {
    "i": 12,
    "start": 41.92333333333333,
    "end": 45.66345833333333,
    "text": "And somewhere in the world, a person they don't know will die."
   },
   {
    "i": 13,
    "start": 45.82666666666666,
    "end": 47.591583333333325,
    "text": "But who he works for, he won't say."
   },
   {
    "i": 14,
    "start": 48.21666666666666,
    "end": 52.21966666666666,
    "text": "Arthur ends the conversation, sends the man away, and tears up the card he left behind."
   },
   {
    "i": 15,
    "start": 53.00666666666666,
    "end": 55.66229166666666,
    "text": "But Norma can't stop thinking about the box."
   },
   {
    "i": 16,
    "start": 55.846666666666664,
    "end": 59.186375,
    "text": "The next day, she pieces the card back together and calls Steward."
   },
   {
    "i": 17,
    "start": 59.666666666666664,
    "end": 63.823375,
    "text": "The man repeats that they won't know the person who dies, and they won't see them die."
   },
   {
    "i": 18,
    "start": 64.55666666666666,
    "end": 67.03220833333333,
    "text": "That evening, the package shows up at their door again."
   },
   {
    "i": 19,
    "start": 67.35666666666665,
    "end": 69.63125,
    "text": "Norma takes the box and hides it in the cabinet."
   },
   {
    "i": 20,
    "start": 69.8,
    "end": 71.47449999999999,
    "text": "At dinner, she brings it up."
   },
   {
    "i": 21,
    "start": 71.63666666666666,
    "end": 73.42983333333332,
    "text": "What if the offer is real?"
   },
   {
    "i": 22,
    "start": 73.60666666666665,
    "end": 75.23208333333332,
    "text": "For Arthur, the answer doesn't change."
   },
   {
    "i": 23,
    "start": 75.53666666666666,
    "end": 77.94562499999999,
    "text": "Not knowing the victim won't change what they'd be doing."
   },
   {
    "i": 24,
    "start": 79.13666666666666,
    "end": 87.63316666666665,
    "text": "Norma, though, thinks about everything she's put off for years: the trip to Europe, the little house on the island, the chance of having a child someday."
   },
   {
    "i": 25,
    "start": 87.79316666666665,
    "end": 91.10308333333332,
    "text": "The next morning, once Arthur leaves for work, she takes out the box."
   },
   {
    "i": 26,
    "start": 91.28666666666665,
    "end": 93.80662499999998,
    "text": "She opens the glass cover and presses the button."
   },
   {
    "i": 27,
    "start": 93.97666666666666,
    "end": 94.78604166666666,
    "text": "Nothing happens."
   },
   {
    "i": 28,
    "start": 95.26666666666667,
    "end": 98.34579166666667,
    "text": "Norma decides it's all nonsense and throws the box in the trash."
   },
   {
    "i": 29,
    "start": 98.97666666666666,
    "end": 101.259625,
    "text": "But that evening, a call comes from a hospital."
   },
   {
    "i": 30,
    "start": 101.92666666666666,
    "end": 107.600625,
    "text": "In the crowd on a subway platform, Arthur was pushed in front of a train, and he lost his life."
   },
   {
    "i": 31,
    "start": 107.78,
    "end": 111.15575,
    "text": "In that moment, Norma remembers the insurance."
   },
   {
    "i": 32,
    "start": 111.31666666666668,
    "end": 119.08820833333334,
    "text": "Her husband's twenty-five-thousand-dollar life insurance pays double for accidental death: exactly fifty thousand dollars."
   },
   {
    "i": 33,
    "start": 119.25,
    "end": 122.01720833333333,
    "text": "She pulls the box out of the trash and breaks it open."
   },
   {
    "i": 34,
    "start": 122.17720833333333,
    "end": 124.73362499999999,
    "text": "There are no wires inside, and no mechanism."
   },
   {
    "i": 35,
    "start": 124.89362499999999,
    "end": 127.18149999999999,
    "text": "The box is completely empty."
   },
   {
    "i": 36,
    "start": 127.34666666666666,
    "end": 128.79129166666667,
    "text": "The phone rings again."
   },
   {
    "i": 37,
    "start": 128.95129166666666,
    "end": 129.986125,
    "text": "It's Steward."
   },
   {
    "i": 38,
    "start": 130.20999999999998,
    "end": 133.80866666666665,
    "text": "Norma screams that they told her she wouldn't know the person who'd die."
   },
   {
    "i": 39,
    "start": 133.96999999999997,
    "end": 137.13441666666662,
    "text": "Steward asks her whether she ever really knew her husband."
   },
   {
    "i": 40,
    "start": 138.08999999999997,
    "end": 146.828625,
    "text": "For Norma, the person who would pay the price was a distant, nameless stranger. But every stranger was someone else's nearest and dearest."
   }
  ],
